Z||000009||Dumba$$||08-14-2001||10:53 PM||||for front bumper parking /turning signal<BR>you could use some from an 86ish pontiac 6000 same light (i think) butt there clear lenses, and use an orange bulb that is what i was thinking of doing <P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE soon to be 4.9<BR>98 acura cl 3.0||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||08-15-2001||12:03 AM||||Damn Jaei Sun....impressive!!!  Yeah, Scott's my buddy here at school.  I'm working at making my fiero faster/better handling than his Beretta so he'll stop feeling so big headed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Here's a link to what I'm talking about...close to the notchback, except more like altezzas and less like torn apart taillights:<P> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/super/ghettoretta/alteeza.htm" TARGET=_blank>Scott's AltEEza Taillights</A><P>As far as having clear blinker/side marker lights...those are *much* easier than tail lights.  You can either find some clear ones off an old car that are clear, or get some aftermarket.  The easiest way is to buy some aftermarket clear ones (cool looking, just like the Audi/VW ones) and attach them to a small plate the same size as the old light to fill the hole.  There are lots of more in-depth ways to get rid of a "filler panel" but the easiest way is to create the filler.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>P.S.  Jaei..how do you know Scott?  You have a Beretta too?<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000011||Jimmy||08-15-2001||12:15 AM||||Jaei Sun also has a black berreta with homemade alteezas.  Sound Identical to the one mentioned above.<P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jaei Sun||08-15-2001||01:01 AM||||I'm on the Beretta.net message board (yeah believe it or not they have a board), and I was the first person to make the alteeza's in question.  I made them around January/Febuary of this year.  I posted a few pictures of them on Beretta net and I guess since then others have made them too.<P>  A long while back I talked with Scott (thru e-mail) about upgrading the computer in my Beretta, he's a pretty cool guy.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Nashco||08-15-2001||02:09 AM||||Haha..that's funny..I just assumed this was an original idea.  So, were you the one to use the "Alteeza" name first, or was that his idea?  Yeah, he's a good guy...he tries to be knowledgeable and learn as much as he can.  He'll be the first guy to say he doesn't know if that's the case, rather than pretending like he knows everything.  How do you like your lights?  They look pretty good for what they are, that's for sure.  The blue film was a great touch..makes them look even more real at night.  The beretta.net is ok...too many bickerers over there (I hate to see our forum lean that way at all).  Did you ever see his air condioned intake post on beretta.net?  That was a riot!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000014||Jaei Sun||08-15-2001||02:20 AM||||Actually Alteeza is the name of the style of taillights... I guess Toyota/Lexus is the creator of the name.  Mine turned out fantastic, but I made mine quite a bit different then Scott did.  Used different lenses.<P>It seems on the bnet board that there are also alot more kids that don't know anything about cars there.  And have been watching too many K&N commercials about how much "power" just a different filter can give a car... LOL!||||reg||4
Z||000015||Nashco||08-15-2001||02:33 AM||||Actually....the real lenses are called "Altezza" after the Toyota Altezza.  Scott calls his Alteezas because they're a tease..they're not real altezzas.  Ha..haha...get it...alTEEza!  Yeah, the beretta.net has too many know it alls, you're right.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000016||8Ball||08-15-2001||11:26 AM||||ok so if the clear tail lights are so easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Anyone wanna either tell me how or point me to a link that tells how to do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||08-15-2001||11:44 AM||||Anyone try this with a GT? All the pics I've seen are on coupes...?||||reg||1
Z||000018||Loki||08-15-2001||12:02 PM||||Remove red lens and add red bulbs   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Nice but around here will get you pulled over in a heart beat.. Illegal like a mofo. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000019||qwikgta||08-15-2001||12:47 PM||||8ball,<BR>  First remove the taillight assembaly. (the six small black squares, and six bolts)  Remove lights.  The taillight ass is held together with some small clips and glue.   You will see two clips on top, and three on bottom (or vise/versa)  VERY carefully pry them up and pull the taillight ass apart.  then remove the clear and red lens.  Put it back together, reglue it and put in red bulbs.  Takes about 15-30 min each side.<P>Rob||||reg||1
